  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled) -> agent frontmatter is `mcpServers: [brain]`; Remaining-work -> "Every agent definition under `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/` that declares `mcpServers: [obsidian]` becomes `mcpServers: [brain]`."
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/install/installAgents/.aide` outcomes.undesired ("An install that wires Obsidian MCP inline in every agent's mcpServers field with full connection config..."): again names "Obsidian MCP" — should read "the brain MCP." The structural rule (declare by name reference, not inline config) still holds; the name has changed.
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/install/installAgents/.aide` Strategy ("Agents declare MCP servers by name reference, not inline config. An agent that needs Obsidian declares `mcpServers: [obsidian]`. The host project's `.mcp.json` provides the actual Obsidian server config..."): the example pin `mcpServers: [obsidian]` is now stale — the canonical declaration is `mcpServers: [brain]` because the MCP key is fixed at `brain` regardless of which backend the host project wired underneath it.
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/install/installAgents/.aide` Strategy ("AIDE is opinionated about the knowledge layer: Obsidian MCP is the brain. The domain expert writes to it..."): "Obsidian MCP is the brain" pins one backend as the canonical brain. The handoff settled that the brain layer is backend-agnostic — Obsidian is one driver in the registry, not the singular brain. The strategy paragraph teaches the wrong abstraction.
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled) -> backend identity inferred from command/args shape; "the brain owns its own navigation rules after the entry-point" — agnostic about which backend is wired.
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/install/installAgents/.aide` Bad example ("An agent file that hardcodes `d:/Code/Me/my-brain` as the vault path. The host project has a different vault. The agent fails on first brain access."): the example is correct in shape but the surrounding paragraphs frame it as Obsidian-specific. The post-handoff framing should be backend-agnostic.
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

