## Retro

### Cycle 4 (post-schema-collapse)

The schema-collapse refactor (Apr 24-26) retired the brainBackends
registry and every package-level notion of "backend identity," but
this spec was not re-walked. The fixed-`brain`-key cycle correctly
updated agent frontmatter from `[obsidian]` to `[brain]`, but the
*explanation* — Strategy paragraphs, Context, and Bad examples — still
frames the abstraction as "the agent declares `[brain]` so the host
can wire any backend underneath." The post-collapse model is stronger:
the package has no concept of "backend" at all; the user wires whatever
they wire, and the helper has no opinion about it. The spec's invariants
(declare by name, never inline config, never hardcode vault paths) are
still correct; the *frame* that explains why teaches a model the root
spec retired. Pattern matches `feedback_schema_collapse_amplifies_cascade.md`:
once-aligned specs accumulate fossil framings during multi-axis root
revisions even when their behavioral invariants are still load-bearing.

The fix is a `/aide:spec` pass that rewrites Context, Strategy, and the
Bad-example explanation to drop "backend driver underneath," "Obsidian
today, others tomorrow," and "regardless of which backend" — replacing
them with framing that reflects the user-owned brain.aide model.

### Cycle 3 (prior — agent rename + post-move)
